{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race telemetry or Evaluator feedback, so this is a conservative baseline meant to finish the course and produce measurements. Geometry: five sensors spaced 12 mm apart across x = -0.024 to +0.024 m, 0.05 m ahead of the axle, with 12 mm footprints so neighbouring sensors overlap and the 25 mm tape is always covered by at least two or three sensors. Sensors sit ahead of the axle so the controller reacts before the wheels reach a bend. Weights are the sensor x-offsets in units of 12 mm ([-2,-1,0,1,2]), so the signal is roughly the tape's lateral offset in those units (range ±2). Controller: kp = 2.0 gives about 700 PWM of differential per unit of signal, enough to turn back on a moderate bend without saturating on small errors. ki = 0 avoids integral windup on long bends. kd = 0.2 damps the oscillation a proportional-only loop tends to produce at speed. base_speed = 1.6 (80% of full PWM) targets the roughly 1.5 m/s average needed to finish in under 3 s while leaving margin for slowing in bends. line_loss = last_direction, so the robot keeps turning the way it was heading when it lost the tape. Geometry is 0.12 m track, 0.03 m wheel radius, 0.12 m body width, 0.16 m length and 0.8 kg mass: a mid-sized, stable yaw inertia. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with some oscillation on the slalom. The next race should show whether kp or kd is too high (steering_oscillation, max_error) and whether the speed is high enough (completion_time). Hypotheses to test: (1) 1.6 base speed completes within 3 s; (2) kp=2 is not oscillating; (3) the line is never lost on the development tracks. Measurements requested: all available metrics, so the next iteration can separate speed, tracking error and oscillation.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.024, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.012, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.012, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.024, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 2.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 0.2,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "Baseline candidate with no prior race data: five 12 mm sensors spaced 12 mm apart, kp=2, kd=0.2, ki=0, base_speed 1.6, last_direction line loss. Chosen to finish the course and expose speed, tracking and oscillation for the next iteration."
    }
  }
}
